## How to use Safe Exam Browser

For assessments which require Safe Exam Browser, you must have the browser installed on your system.

1. Download Safe Exam Browser: <a href="https://safeexambrowser.org/download_en.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Safe Exam Browser - Download Latest Releases</a>

![Safe Exam Browser Download](https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/static.bytexl.app/uploads/3yq4w6g9z/content/3zysw5zgr/seb-download-001.png)

2. Install & Open Test Page: Once installed, download the .seb file (using the button above).

3. Open .seb File: .seb files are entry points to Safe Exam Browser. Your system should automatically open .seb files with Safe Exam Browser. If not, set Safe Exam Browser as the default application for .seb files.

4. Login: Upon opening, you'll be asked to login with your bytexl credentials. The Safe Exam Browser application will not allow you to access any other application in your system without exiting the assessment.

**Note:** Make sure you have your bytexl credentials handy before starting the assessment.
`;function sZt({test:r,token:e}){const t=bl(),n=()=>{FI.downloadSebFile(r,e)};return I.useEffect(()=>{Jg(t,"seb_dnd_page_view",{test:r})},[r]),f.createElement(j,{sx:{width:"100%",textAlign:"center",pt:4}},f.createElement(K,{variant:"h1",gutterBottom:!0},"Browser Not Allowed!"),f.createElement(K,{variant:"body1",sx:{color:"text.secondary",mb:4}},"Please use Safe Exam Browser to take the ",r?.title||""," test."),f.createElement(j,null,f.createElement(Ke,{variant:"contained",color:"primary",sx:{mr:2},onClick:n,endIcon:f.createElement(jf,null)},"Download SEB File"),f.createElement(Ke,{variant:"outlined",color:"secondary",href:"/"},"Back to Home")),f.createElement(j,{sx:{mt:5,mx:"auto",maxWidth:"60%",p:3,bgcolor:"background.paper",borderRadius:2,boxShadow:2,textAlign:"left"}},f.createElement(Es,{markdown:oZt})))}const lZt=`
## SEB File Modified - Please Re-download

The Safe Exam Browser configuration file appears to have been altered or modified. For security reasons, you cannot proceed with the test using a modified configuration.

### What to do:

1. **Download Fresh SEB File**: Click the "Download SEB File" button above to get a new, unmodified configuration file.

2. **Close Current SEB Session**: Exit the current Safe Exam Browser session completely.

3. **Open New SEB File**: Open the newly downloaded .seb file to start a fresh session.

4. **Contact Support**: If you continue to see this message after downloading a fresh file, please contact your instructor or technical support.

### Why this happens:

- The SEB configuration file may have been accidentally modified
- Network issues during download might have corrupted the file
